            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1800' id='32' type-v2='text' w='99364' x='91' y='57575'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='12'>Note: The graphs to see the performance over time were included after 2023.07.03, so all the test before that date will not have time series data.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='725' id='33' name='Confidence Intervals Metric Title' show-title='false' w='24000' x='42000' y='69525'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='7375' id='34' name='Time Series Metric Title' show-title='false' w='2727' x='455' y='74700'>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1650' id='35' type-v2='text' w='96000' x='909' y='70375'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000'>In this confidence interval graph you can see the distribution of the metric across the control and treatment group, ideally if the bars are separated it means that with a confidence of 95% the means are going to be different, meanwhile if they overlap that means that they might not be significantly different.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='1025' id='36' type-v2='text' w='95818' x='1000' y='83150'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>In the above this graph you will see the evolution over the timeframe of the ab test for a particular metric in a particular country.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2050' id='37' type-v2='text' w='95818' x='818' y='94300'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>In the above this graph you will see the evolution over the timeframe of the ab test of the count of registers for each metric and model version. (eg. num order per day, num requests per day). 

Ideally each day should maintain the split ratio among Control and Experimental group.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
